hadiths[20]{hadithnumber,text}:
"21561","Waki' narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from 'Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn 'Aqil, from al-Tufayl ibn Ubayy ibn Ka'b, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The quaking came, followed by the following. Death came with what is in it."
"21562","Waki' narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from 'Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn 'Aqil, from al-Tufayl ibn Ubayy ibn Ka'b, from his father, he said: A man said: O Messenger of Allah, what if I make all my prayer upon you? He said: Then Allah, Blessed and Exalted, will suffice you what concerns you of your world and your Hereafter."
"21563","'Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi and Abu 'Amir said: Zuhayr, meaning ibn Muhammad, narrated to us, from 'Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn 'Aqil, from al-Tufayl ibn Ubayy ibn Ka'b, from his father, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: My likeness among the prophets is like a man who built a house, and made it good and perfected it, and left in it the place of a brick he did not lay. So people began circumambulating the building and admiring it, saying: If only the place of this brick were completed. So I among the prophets am the place of that brick."
"21564","Sa'id ibn al-Ash'ath ibn Sa'id al-Samman ibn Abi al-Rabi' narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Salamah, meaning ibn Abi al-Husam, informed us, 'Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn 'Aqil narrated to us, from al-Tufayl ibn Ubayy ibn Ka'b, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: My likeness among the prophets is like a man who built a house, and made it good, and beautified it, and completed it, and left of it the place of a brick he did not lay. So people began circumambulating the building and admiring, saying: If only the place of this brick were completed."
"21565","Abu 'Amir narrated to us, Zuhayr, meaning ibn Muhammad, narrated to us, from 'Abdullah ibn Muhammad, from al-Tufayl ibn Ubayy ibn Ka'b, from his father, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: When it is the Day of Resurrection, I will be the imam of the prophets, and their speaker, and the holder of their intercession, without pride."
"21566","He said: And I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Were it not for the Hijrah, I would be a man of the Ansar. And if people took a valley or a mountain pass, I would be with the Ansar."
"21567","Zakariyya narrated to us, 'Ubaydullah ibn 'Amr narrated to us, from 'Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn 'Aqil, from al-Tufayl ibn Ubayy ibn Ka'b, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When it is the Day of Resurrection, I will be the imam of the prophets, and he mentioned its meaning."
"21568","Zakariyya ibn 'Adi narrated to us, 'Ubaydullah ibn 'Amr informed us, from 'Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn 'Aqil, from al-Tufayl ibn Ubayy ibn Ka'b, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to draw near to a trunk when the mosque was a trellis, and he used to preach to that trunk. A man of his Companions said: O Messenger of Allah, may we make for you something to stand upon on Friday, so people see you and hear your sermon? He said: Yes. So three steps were made for him, those that are upon the minbar. When the minbar was made and placed in the place the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, placed it, when he wanted to come to the minbar he passed by it. When he passed it, the trunk groaned until it cracked and split. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, returned and wiped it with his hand until it calmed. Then he returned to the minbar. And when he prayed, he prayed to it. When the mosque was demolished and changed, Ubayy ibn Ka'b took that trunk, and it was with him until it wore out, and the termites ate it, and it returned to dust."
"21569","Abu Ahmad al-Zubayri narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from 'Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn 'Aqil, from al-Tufayl ibn Ubayy ibn Ka'b, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When it is the Day of Resurrection, I will be the imam of people, and their speaker, and the holder of their intercession, and no pride."
"21570","Ahmad ibn 'Abd al-Malik narrated to us, 'Ubaydullah ibn 'Amr narrated to us, from 'Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn 'Aqil, from Jabir ibn 'Abdullah, he said: While we were rows behind the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, in Zuhr or 'Asr, we saw him reaching for something before him while in prayer, to take it. Then he reached to take it. Then it was prevented between him and it. Then he stepped back, and we stepped back. Then he stepped back a second time, and we stepped back. When he gave salam, Ubayy ibn Ka'b, may Allah be pleased with him, said: O Messenger of Allah, we saw you today doing in your prayer something you never used to do. He said: Paradise was shown to me, with what is in it of splendor, and I reached for a cluster of its grapes to bring to you. Had I taken it, those between heaven and earth would eat of it, and they would not diminish it. And it was prevented between me and it. And Hell was shown to me. When I felt the heat of its flame, I stepped back. And most of those I saw in it were women, who, if trusted, disclose, and if they ask, insist. My father said: Zakariyya ibn 'Adi said: Persist, and if given, do not thank. And I saw in it Luhayy ibn 'Amr dragging his intestines. And the most resembling of those I saw to him was Ma'bad ibn Aktham. Ma'bad said: O Messenger of Allah, is harm feared for me from his resemblance, for he is a father? He said: No, you are a believer, and he is a disbeliever. And he is the first who gathered the Arabs upon idols."
"21571","Ahmad ibn 'Abd al-Malik narrated to us, 'Ubaydullah, meaning ibn 'Amr, narrated to us, 'Abdullah ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from al-Tufayl ibn Ubayy, from his father, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, the like of it."
"21572","Sa'id ibn Abi al-Rabi' al-Samman informed us, Sa'id ibn Salamah ibn Abi al-Husam al-Madini informed me, 'Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn 'Aqil ibn Abi Talib narrated to us, from al-Tufayl ibn Ubayy, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to pray to a trunk when the mosque was a trellis, and he used to preach to people beside that trunk. A man of his Companions said: O Messenger of Allah, may I make for you a minbar to stand upon on Friday, so people see your sermon? He said: Yes. So three steps were made for him, which are upon the minbar. When the minbar was finished and placed in the place the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, placed it, it occurred to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, to stand upon that minbar. So he walked to it. When he passed the trunk he used to preach to and stand to, that trunk groaned to him until it cracked and split. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, descended when he heard the voice of the trunk, and wiped it with his hand. Then he returned to the minbar. And when he prayed with that, he inclined to the trunk. Al-Tufayl says: When the mosque was demolished and changed, his father Ubayy ibn Ka'b took that trunk, and it was with him in his house until it wore out, and the termites ate it, and it returned to dust."
"21573","Hashim ibn al-Harith narrated to us, 'Ubaydullah ibn 'Amr narrated to us, from 'Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn 'Aqil, from al-Tufayl, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When it is the Day of Resurrection, I will be the imam of the prophets, and their speaker, and the holder of their intercession, without pride."
"21574","And he said: Were it not for the Hijrah, I would be a man of the Ansar. And if the Ansar took a valley, or he said: a mountain pass, I would be of the Ansar."
"21575","Abdullah narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Qaza'ah Abu 'Ali al-Basri narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Habib narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Thuwayr, from his father, from al-Tufayl, from his father, that he heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: And He imposed upon them the word of piety. He said: There is no god but Allah."
"21576","'Ubaydullah ibn 'Umar al-Qawariri narrated to us, Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from 'Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn 'Aqil, from al-Tufayl ibn Ubayy ibn Ka'b, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When it is the Day of Resurrection, I will be the imam of the prophets, and their speaker, and the holder of their intercession, and no pride."
"21577","Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to us, Abu Hudhayfah Musa narrated to us, from Zuhayr ibn Muhammad, from 'Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn 'Aqil, from al-Tufayl ibn Ubayy, from his father, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Were it not for the Hijrah, I would be a man of the Ansar. And if the Ansar took a valley or a mountain pass, I would be with the Ansar."
"21578","Zakariyya ibn 'Adi narrated to us, and Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Ahmad ibn 'Abd al-Malik al-Harrani narrated to us, 'Ubaydullah ibn 'Amr narrated to us, from 'Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn 'Aqil, from al-Tufayl ibn Ubayy, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Were it not for the Hijrah, I would be a man of the Ansar. And if people took a mountain pass, or he said: a valley, I would be with the Ansar."
"21579","And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When it is the Day of Resurrection, I will be the imam of the prophets, and their speaker, and the holder of their intercession, without pride. And the hadith is upon the wording of Zakariyya ibn 'Adi."
"21580","Abdullah said: 'Isa ibn Salim Abu Sa'id al-Shashi narrated to us in the year two hundred and thirty, 'Ubaydullah ibn 'Amr, meaning al-Raqqi Abu Wahb, narrated to us, from 'Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn 'Aqil, from al-Tufayl ibn Ubayy ibn Ka'b, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to pray to a trunk, and the mosque was a trellis, and he used to preach beside that trunk. Men of his Companions said: O Messenger of Allah, we will make for you something to stand upon on Friday, so people see, or he said: so people see you, and so people hear your sermon. He said: Yes. So three steps were made for him. The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, stood as he used to stand. The trunk inclined to him. He said to it: Be still. Then he said to his Companions: This trunk yearned to me. The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to it: Be still, if you wish I plant you in Paradise, and the righteous eat of you, and if you wish I return you as you were, moist. So it chose the Hereafter over the world. When the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, passed away, it was given to Ubayy, and it remained with him until the termites ate it."
